1
00:00:05,746 --> 00:00:11,160
Picture a single bowl of liquid, set down
where many kinds of beings can see it.

2
00:00:11,963 --> 00:00:14,940
A human sees clear, refreshing water.

3
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:19,179
A hungry ghost, a being driven
by deep habits of craving,

4
00:00:19,259 --> 00:00:21,421
sees foul pus and blood.

5
00:00:21,501 --> 00:00:25,266
A fish finds the air it breathes
and the home it swims in.

6
00:00:25,346 --> 00:00:27,481
A god tastes heavenly nectar.

7
00:00:27,561 --> 00:00:31,149
And an awakened being sees
the pure wisdom of water,

8
00:00:31,229 --> 00:00:33,572
the female Buddha Māmakī.

9
00:00:34,373 --> 00:00:38,912
It is one of the oldest examples in
Indian and Tibetan Buddhist thought.

10
00:00:38,992 --> 00:00:42,381
And it asks a simple question.
What is really in the bowl?

11
00:00:43,185 --> 00:00:45,251
Common sense has a ready answer.

12
00:00:45,331 --> 00:00:49,436
Something must be sitting there
first, some raw and neutral stuff.

13
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:52,126
Each creature looks at
it through its own lens.

14
00:00:52,206 --> 00:00:56,166
Two layers: the hidden thing,
and the many views of it.

15
00:00:56,965 --> 00:01:00,716
The Middle Way of Nāgārjuna,
and the Great Perfection,

16
00:01:00,796 --> 00:01:05,784
Dzogchen, read without a foundation,
both take this picture apart.

17
00:01:05,864 --> 00:01:08,461
Agreement does not need a hidden bedrock.

18
00:01:08,541 --> 00:01:13,964
The thing seen, the one seeing, and the
way they meet are identified together,

19
00:01:14,044 --> 00:01:15,893
each depending on the others.

20
00:01:15,973 --> 00:01:20,608
And the relations between them are just
as impossible to pin down as the things

21
00:01:20,688 --> 00:01:21,888
themselves.

22
00:01:22,697 --> 00:01:26,638
Start with a word we slipped in
without noticing. The liquid.

23
00:01:26,718 --> 00:01:31,584
To say that beings see the same liquid
differently already assumes an object

24
00:01:31,664 --> 00:01:35,905
waiting there, with its own
identity, before anyone meets it.

25
00:01:35,985 --> 00:01:39,125
This is the old idea
that Kant made famous:

26
00:01:39,205 --> 00:01:42,580
a thing in itself,
hidden behind the senses.

27
00:01:43,389 --> 00:01:45,646
So ask what this hidden thing is like.

28
00:01:45,726 --> 00:01:49,980
If it has definite qualities, if it
really is thirst-quenching water,

29
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:53,445
it cannot explain why the
ghost meets burning pus.

30
00:01:53,525 --> 00:01:57,901
If it has no qualities at all, a
featureless blank cannot set off any

31
00:01:57,981 --> 00:02:01,384
experience. Either way, it does no work.

32
00:02:02,185 --> 00:02:03,626
Someone will push back.

33
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:08,178
Why not simply wetness, the
quality that water and pus share?

34
00:02:08,258 --> 00:02:11,738
But wetness in general is
an idea made by thought.

35
00:02:11,818 --> 00:02:16,004
In real life it only ever shows
up as this drinkable water,

36
00:02:16,084 --> 00:02:19,578
this foul pus, this water a fish lives in.

37
00:02:19,658 --> 00:02:23,219
And if wetness is only an
agreed point of comparison,

38
00:02:23,299 --> 00:02:27,218
it is no longer a hidden thing
at all. It is a useful label.

39
00:02:28,050 --> 00:02:33,093
What Nāgārjuna's analysis targets
is called svabhāva, own nature.

40
00:02:33,173 --> 00:02:37,658
It means a nature a thing would have
all by itself, depending on nothing.

41
00:02:37,738 --> 00:02:42,468
A neutral substance beneath appearances
is that same imagined nature,

42
00:02:42,548 --> 00:02:44,306
in a modest disguise.

43
00:02:45,118 --> 00:02:47,104
Then a real question remains.

44
00:02:47,184 --> 00:02:51,669
If there is no hidden object, why do
humans agree so reliably that the liquid

45
00:02:51,749 --> 00:02:57,176
is water? Why doesn't the shared world
fall apart into private fantasies?

46
00:02:57,997 --> 00:03:01,517
The Indian master
Candrakīrti answers plainly.

47
00:03:01,597 --> 00:03:04,126
Agreement does not prove a hidden object.

48
00:03:04,206 --> 00:03:09,076
Shared, reliable agreement is
simply what everyday truth is.

49
00:03:09,894 --> 00:03:12,382
He also refuses the opposite move.

50
00:03:12,462 --> 00:03:17,029
The Mind-Only school tried to solve the
puzzle by removing outer objects and

51
00:03:17,109 --> 00:03:19,909
making consciousness the real foundation.

52
00:03:19,989 --> 00:03:23,483
But a seeing cannot be
identified without what is seen.

53
00:03:23,563 --> 00:03:27,871
And an object cannot be identified
without the seeing that picks it out.

54
00:03:27,951 --> 00:03:30,629
Neither mind nor matter comes first.

55
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:35,562
Making the mind the container of
everything is as mistaken as making matter

56
00:03:35,642 --> 00:03:36,842
the container.

57
00:03:37,594 --> 00:03:40,762
Within everyday truth,
mistakes are still caught.

58
00:03:40,842 --> 00:03:44,457
A person with jaundice sees a
white conch shell as yellow,

59
00:03:44,537 --> 00:03:46,930
and people with healthy eyes correct them.

60
00:03:47,010 --> 00:03:49,145
But notice where that judgement is made.

61
00:03:49,225 --> 00:03:51,577
It is made within one kind of being.

62
00:03:51,657 --> 00:03:54,579
The hungry ghost is not a jaundiced human.

63
00:03:54,659 --> 00:03:58,724
By the standards of its own
kind, its senses work normally.

64
00:03:58,804 --> 00:04:02,587
For the ghost, the liquid
really does function as pus.

65
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:05,027
So what of the bowl itself?

66
00:04:05,107 --> 00:04:08,682
What is denied is a shared
base that exists by itself,

67
00:04:08,762 --> 00:04:11,019
there before anyone perceives it.

68
00:04:11,099 --> 00:04:13,356
What is kept is a working reference point.

69
00:04:13,436 --> 00:04:16,562
It is a label, made from within one frame,

70
00:04:16,642 --> 00:04:20,978
for the place where different ways of
appearing meet and can be compared.

71
00:04:21,058 --> 00:04:24,502
Its job is to coordinate,
not to sit underneath.

72
00:04:25,314 --> 00:04:28,264
The bowl example did not
begin in the Middle Way.

73
00:04:28,344 --> 00:04:34,344
Vasubandhu, in his Twenty Verses, used
the hungry ghosts to defend Mind-Only.

74
00:04:34,676 --> 00:04:39,582
Ghosts with the same karma all see
a river of pus together, he said.

75
00:04:39,662 --> 00:04:44,935
Shared karma, ripening in consciousness,
explains shared experience.

76
00:04:45,015 --> 00:04:47,453
No river outside the mind is needed.

77
00:04:48,286 --> 00:04:51,902
That answers the question by
making consciousness the floor.

78
00:04:51,982 --> 00:04:54,973
Candrakīrti turned the example around.

79
00:04:55,053 --> 00:04:58,587
If the river of pus is
not established by itself,

80
00:04:58,667 --> 00:05:00,937
neither is the mind that sees it.

81
00:05:01,017 --> 00:05:05,380
The river of pus and the seeing
of it stand or fall together.

82
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:09,225
So the bowl does not show that
the world is inside the mind.

83
00:05:09,305 --> 00:05:13,143
It shows that neither the world
nor the mind is the floor.

84
00:05:13,957 --> 00:05:16,784
Agreement also needs others to agree with.

85
00:05:16,864 --> 00:05:20,697
Indian logicians debated whether
other minds could be proven.

86
00:05:20,777 --> 00:05:24,026
Both sides assumed that my
own experience is certain,

87
00:05:24,106 --> 00:05:25,684
and yours only inferred.

88
00:05:25,764 --> 00:05:28,292
The Middle Way refuses that imbalance.

89
00:05:28,372 --> 00:05:33,089
Looked for closely, my stream of
experience is no more findable than yours,

90
00:05:33,169 --> 00:05:35,276
and both work in daily life.

91
00:05:35,356 --> 00:05:38,759
Other observers are identified
together with this one,

92
00:05:38,848 --> 00:05:41,707
as long is identified together with short.

93
00:05:42,521 --> 00:05:44,289
A critic can press further.

94
00:05:44,369 --> 00:05:48,174
Senses count as healthy when they
agree with others of their kind,

95
00:05:48,254 --> 00:05:52,780
and the kind is defined by sharing
those senses. Isn't that circular?

96
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:55,471
It is, and the circle is not a flaw.

97
00:05:55,551 --> 00:05:59,683
It would be fatal only if agreement
had to rest on a final judge,

98
00:05:59,763 --> 00:06:01,911
outside every point of view.

99
00:06:01,991 --> 00:06:03,636
There is no such judge.

100
00:06:03,716 --> 00:06:07,214
Wittgenstein reached a similar
point from another direction:

101
00:06:07,317 --> 00:06:11,870
we agree, not in opinions,
but in a shared form of life.

102
00:06:11,950 --> 00:06:15,158
And inside the circle,
correction is still real.

103
00:06:15,238 --> 00:06:17,432
A second look corrects a misreading.

104
00:06:18,277 --> 00:06:22,165
For humans, much of this
agreement is carried by language.

105
00:06:22,245 --> 00:06:25,208
A child learns the word
water because it works.

106
00:06:25,288 --> 00:06:27,505
Say it, and a glass arrives.

107
00:06:27,585 --> 00:06:32,409
Yet language is also where the habit
of making things solid is strongest.

108
00:06:32,489 --> 00:06:38,419
The noun, the bowl, seems to point at
one solid thing behind every view of it.

109
00:06:39,227 --> 00:06:43,418
Dzogchen describes the same freedom
from the side of experience.

110
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:47,377
In the Dzogchen of Longchenpa and Mipham,

111
00:06:47,457 --> 00:06:50,126
the basis is primordially pure.

112
00:06:50,215 --> 00:06:53,382
From the very beginning,
appearing was never fixed,

113
00:06:53,462 --> 00:06:55,692
so nothing ever needed cleaning.

114
00:06:55,772 --> 00:06:58,627
The basis is not a hidden block of stuff,

115
00:06:58,707 --> 00:07:01,969
a cosmic mind, or a
starting point of the world.

116
00:07:02,049 --> 00:07:06,426
Longchenpa says it is called a ground
only from a relative point of view.

117
00:07:06,506 --> 00:07:10,656
In the way things are, it is
empty of being any ground at all.

118
00:07:11,457 --> 00:07:13,415
Appearances are called display.

119
00:07:13,495 --> 00:07:17,192
And display is not the display
of something standing behind it.

120
00:07:17,272 --> 00:07:23,272
It is dependent arising itself, vivid
and unobstructed, with nothing behind it.

121
00:07:23,468 --> 00:07:26,309
Even the feeling of
being a subject inside,

122
00:07:26,389 --> 00:07:29,461
looking out at a world,
is part of the display.

123
00:07:29,541 --> 00:07:32,849
It arises together with the
world it seems to look at.

124
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:38,350
Knowing awareness, rigpa, is not
a projector throwing out a world.

125
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:40,823
It is not a subtle stuff behind appearing,

126
00:07:40,903 --> 00:07:42,575
and it is not the basis.

127
00:07:42,655 --> 00:07:47,018
It is the knowing of the basis:
knowing appearing as unfixed,

128
00:07:47,098 --> 00:07:48,771
dependent and empty.

129
00:07:48,851 --> 00:07:51,882
The clarity belongs to
the appearing itself.

130
00:07:51,962 --> 00:07:54,360
And like the appearing, it is empty.

131
00:07:55,169 --> 00:07:57,004
Does awareness know itself?

132
00:07:57,084 --> 00:08:00,768
Candrakīrti refused a
self-knowing consciousness:

133
00:08:00,848 --> 00:08:04,178
a blade, he said, cannot cut itself.

134
00:08:04,258 --> 00:08:08,526
In Dzogchen, the self-knowing
of awareness is no second act,

135
00:08:08,606 --> 00:08:11,108
and no knower watching from behind.

136
00:08:11,188 --> 00:08:15,415
It is simply clarity, recognised
as belonging to no one,

137
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:17,838
and empty like everything else.

138
00:08:18,645 --> 00:08:22,790
Mipham also separates ordinary
vision from pure vision.

139
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:28,021
Within ordinary vision, no kind of
being has the last word over another.

140
00:08:28,101 --> 00:08:30,385
Even the gods' nectar belongs here.

141
00:08:30,465 --> 00:08:34,167
In pure vision, the
liquid appears as Māmakī.

142
00:08:34,256 --> 00:08:37,586
But pure vision is not
a window onto a bedrock.

143
00:08:37,666 --> 00:08:40,182
Māmakī has no nature of her own.

144
00:08:40,262 --> 00:08:44,733
Pure vision is clearer because it meets
appearing without the habit that splits it

145
00:08:44,813 --> 00:08:47,917
into a solid self and solid things.

146
00:08:48,721 --> 00:08:51,630
Modern physics offers echoes of all this.

147
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:53,958
Only echoes, not proofs.

148
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:57,682
For the physicist and
philosopher Karen Barad,

149
00:08:57,762 --> 00:09:01,079
things do not exist
first and then interact.

150
00:09:01,159 --> 00:09:03,932
They emerge through what
she calls intra-action.

151
00:09:04,012 --> 00:09:06,731
So there is no liquid
waiting before the meeting.

152
00:09:06,811 --> 00:09:09,883
The human drinker and the
water appear together.

153
00:09:09,963 --> 00:09:13,189
The suffering ghost and
the pus appear together.

154
00:09:14,001 --> 00:09:17,059
In Carlo Rovelli's
relational quantum mechanics,

155
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:21,434
physical quantities have values
only relative to another system.

156
00:09:21,514 --> 00:09:24,383
How, then, do two observers agree?

157
00:09:24,463 --> 00:09:30,021
With Emily Adlam, Rovelli answered: when
a second observer interacts with the first

158
00:09:30,101 --> 00:09:33,146
and with what was measured,
their results match.

159
00:09:33,226 --> 00:09:36,298
Agreement comes from
checking across perspectives,

160
00:09:36,378 --> 00:09:38,585
not from a hidden state underneath.

161
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:43,311
But neither theory should be read as
saying that relations are what is really

162
00:09:43,391 --> 00:09:46,287
there. That would only
build another floor.

163
00:09:46,367 --> 00:09:50,241
Relations and the things
related are identified together,

164
00:09:50,321 --> 00:09:52,093
and neither is the ground.

165
00:09:52,913 --> 00:09:55,740
If appearances depend
on channels of contact,

166
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:59,613
what happens when a being shares
almost no channel with something?

167
00:09:59,693 --> 00:10:01,546
Contact comes in degrees.

168
00:10:02,349 --> 00:10:07,092
A tick responds mainly to three
signals: the smell of mammal sweat,

169
00:10:07,172 --> 00:10:09,633
the warmth of a body, and hair.

170
00:10:09,713 --> 00:10:12,853
A pool of clear spring
water has none of these,

171
00:10:12,933 --> 00:10:15,312
so it never appears in the tick's world.

172
00:10:15,392 --> 00:10:17,894
Yet the water is not nothing to the tick.

173
00:10:17,974 --> 00:10:22,717
If the tick falls in, the surface holds
it and the current carries it away.

174
00:10:22,797 --> 00:10:25,951
Dark matter passes through
the Earth without collision,

175
00:10:26,031 --> 00:10:28,953
yet gravity still bends its path.

176
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:34,393
A neutrino can cross vast thicknesses
of lead and almost never touch an atom.

177
00:10:34,509 --> 00:10:37,758
For it, the lead is
neither a wall nor nothing.

178
00:10:37,838 --> 00:10:40,493
It is a region of very weak contact.

179
00:10:41,318 --> 00:10:43,901
So what appears in a meeting, nourishment,

180
00:10:43,981 --> 00:10:49,694
pus, a barrier or an open passage, depends
on which channels are active in it.

181
00:10:50,501 --> 00:10:53,491
The hardest test is
contact between worlds.

182
00:10:53,571 --> 00:10:58,872
In offerings to hungry ghosts, water
is blessed with a mantra and given,

183
00:10:58,952 --> 00:11:02,350
and the tradition holds that
it reaches them as nectar.

184
00:11:02,430 --> 00:11:04,578
Not by a substance that travels.

185
00:11:04,658 --> 00:11:08,220
Nothing passes from the human
bowl into the ghost's mouth,

186
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:13,559
just as nothing passes from the evening
flame of a lamp into its midnight flame.

187
00:11:13,639 --> 00:11:15,991
The giving belongs to the human world.

188
00:11:16,071 --> 00:11:18,342
The relief belongs to the ghost's.

189
00:11:18,422 --> 00:11:23,496
They are linked as condition and result,
with no common object underneath.

190
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:27,070
That the offering helps
is a claim of tradition.

191
00:11:27,150 --> 00:11:29,067
This argument does not prove it.

192
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:33,021
It only shows that such a link
would need no hidden substance.

193
00:11:33,101 --> 00:11:38,157
And physics gives it no support, because
in physics agreement needs real contact

194
00:11:38,237 --> 00:11:39,697
between observers.

195
00:11:40,514 --> 00:11:43,573
Why do we cling so hard
to an object underneath?

196
00:11:43,653 --> 00:11:45,407
Because of the container myth.

197
00:11:45,487 --> 00:11:48,016
We picture space as an empty box.

198
00:11:48,096 --> 00:11:52,663
We place a solid object in the middle, and
put observers around it who must either

199
00:11:52,743 --> 00:11:55,312
see the real thing or be fooled.

200
00:11:55,392 --> 00:11:59,565
In Einstein's theory, spacetime
is not an empty stage.

201
00:11:59,645 --> 00:12:02,078
It is the gravitational field itself.

202
00:12:02,158 --> 00:12:07,255
And Nāgārjuna shows that space cannot
exist before its own defining mark,

203
00:12:07,335 --> 00:12:09,307
the absence of obstruction.

204
00:12:09,387 --> 00:12:14,379
When the box goes, the puzzle of one
object seen many ways goes with it.

205
00:12:15,185 --> 00:12:20,798
One more question. If there is no ultimate
ground, why is the world so orderly?

206
00:12:20,878 --> 00:12:23,696
Barley seeds grow barley, not rice.

207
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:26,137
Fire burns and does not freeze.

208
00:12:26,217 --> 00:12:30,462
Being empty of a fixed nature
does not make anything arbitrary.

209
00:12:31,282 --> 00:12:35,238
But emptiness is not what makes
cause and effect work, either.

210
00:12:35,318 --> 00:12:38,598
Emptiness enables nothing
and explains nothing.

211
00:12:38,701 --> 00:12:41,854
Things never needed a fixed
essence in order to work.

212
00:12:41,934 --> 00:12:45,156
And something with a fixed
essence could never arise,

213
00:12:45,236 --> 00:12:46,900
change or end.

214
00:12:47,713 --> 00:12:52,198
Ask why there is a web of causes at all,
and the question treats the whole web as

215
00:12:52,278 --> 00:12:55,092
one thing that needs an outside cause.

216
00:12:55,172 --> 00:13:00,350
But the whole is a label too, and
dependent arising has no first beginning.

217
00:13:00,430 --> 00:13:04,933
The question does not uncover a
hidden answer. It loses its object.

218
00:13:05,754 --> 00:13:08,654
So far, one bowl. Now widen the view.

219
00:13:09,478 --> 00:13:12,714
If each kind of being meets
the bowl in its own way,

220
00:13:12,794 --> 00:13:15,811
then each lives in a
whole world of its own.

221
00:13:15,891 --> 00:13:20,268
Its own textures, distances,
dangers and nourishment.

222
00:13:20,348 --> 00:13:22,931
Buddhist texts call such a world a loka.

223
00:13:23,011 --> 00:13:27,215
The biologist Jakob von
Uexküll called it an Umwelt.

224
00:13:28,021 --> 00:13:31,011
Worlds are made by channels, not by walls.

225
00:13:31,091 --> 00:13:34,150
The tick lives in a
world of three signals.

226
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:39,503
The bat finds its way by echoes, in
a darkness that is no obstacle to it.

227
00:13:39,583 --> 00:13:44,734
The honeybee sees ultraviolet light, so
flowers that look plain to us carry bright

228
00:13:44,814 --> 00:13:46,419
landing paths for it.

229
00:13:46,499 --> 00:13:49,942
And we live among
colours, words and clocks.

230
00:13:50,753 --> 00:13:53,703
This needs no belief in ghosts or gods.

231
00:13:53,783 --> 00:13:56,366
The animals alone carry the argument.

232
00:13:56,446 --> 00:13:59,821
Those who accept the traditional
realms can extend it to them.

233
00:14:00,621 --> 00:14:02,620
Every world has three sides.

234
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:05,595
A being, with its senses and habits.

235
00:14:05,675 --> 00:14:09,902
An environment, as that being meets
it. And the channels joining them.

236
00:14:09,982 --> 00:14:14,943
None comes first. Even the shared
environment, in the old Buddhist account,

237
00:14:15,023 --> 00:14:18,000
is shaped by the karma
of those who live in it.

238
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:21,197
It is not a box that would
exist with no one inside.

239
00:14:22,009 --> 00:14:24,565
Worlds also overlap by degrees.

240
00:14:24,645 --> 00:14:28,532
A human and a dog share
sight, hearing and touch,

241
00:14:28,612 --> 00:14:30,665
so they can live and play together.

242
00:14:30,745 --> 00:14:34,130
A human and a tick meet
briefly, at the skin.

243
00:14:34,210 --> 00:14:39,352
In the traditional account, a human and
a hungry ghost share almost nothing.

244
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:41,925
Then where are the other worlds?

245
00:14:42,005 --> 00:14:46,626
The tempting answer is: right
here, in the same space as ours.

246
00:14:46,706 --> 00:14:48,406
It sounds open-minded.

247
00:14:48,486 --> 00:14:50,783
But it quietly brings back the box.

248
00:14:50,863 --> 00:14:54,764
It assumes one neutral space
underneath both worlds,

249
00:14:54,844 --> 00:14:56,712
holding them side by side.

250
00:14:57,513 --> 00:15:01,441
Indian and Tibetan logic
knows two kinds of negation.

251
00:15:01,521 --> 00:15:04,552
One denies something and
implies something else.

252
00:15:04,632 --> 00:15:08,411
The other simply denies, and
puts nothing in its place.

253
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:10,721
Emptiness is the second kind.

254
00:15:10,801 --> 00:15:13,425
So we can say the other
worlds are not elsewhere.

255
00:15:13,505 --> 00:15:17,256
Not far away, not behind
a wall. And we stop there.

256
00:15:17,336 --> 00:15:20,408
We do not add, so they
are in the same place.

257
00:15:20,488 --> 00:15:24,217
Each world has its own
here, its own near and far.

258
00:15:25,034 --> 00:15:28,052
Buddhist traditions have
drawn two kinds of map.

259
00:15:28,132 --> 00:15:33,079
The old Abhidharma map stacks the
realms in a vast vertical cosmos,

260
00:15:33,159 --> 00:15:37,604
with a great mountain at its
centre, gods above and hells below.

261
00:15:37,684 --> 00:15:42,074
Other traditions stress that the
realms, and even the pure lands,

262
00:15:42,154 --> 00:15:43,935
are not far away at all.

263
00:15:44,015 --> 00:15:49,524
Read without a container, both are
maps, each useful for its own purpose.

264
00:15:50,345 --> 00:15:52,574
Worlds touch where channels are shared.

265
00:15:52,654 --> 00:15:55,903
A tick reaches a human
through warmth and skin.

266
00:15:55,983 --> 00:15:58,824
A dog and its owner meet in a glance.

267
00:15:58,904 --> 00:16:01,800
What never crosses is a view from nowhere.

268
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:06,501
No being can step outside every world
and compare them all from above.

269
00:16:06,581 --> 00:16:09,626
A human can learn a great
deal about the bat's world,

270
00:16:09,706 --> 00:16:11,315
but always as a human.

271
00:16:12,117 --> 00:16:15,039
So the human world is not the master copy.

272
00:16:15,119 --> 00:16:20,298
It has every practical priority for us,
but no final authority over the bat,

273
00:16:20,378 --> 00:16:22,295
the bee or the ghost.

274
00:16:22,375 --> 00:16:24,224
Science does not escape this.

275
00:16:24,304 --> 00:16:29,143
It extends our senses, with instruments
that reach the bee's ultraviolet and the

276
00:16:29,223 --> 00:16:33,681
neutrino. It is our most
reliable map within its domains.

277
00:16:33,761 --> 00:16:37,163
But every instrument is
built and read by humans.

278
00:16:37,969 --> 00:16:39,804
And this is not relativism.

279
00:16:39,884 --> 00:16:43,772
Within every world there are still
mistakes, like the jaundiced eye.

280
00:16:43,852 --> 00:16:48,573
And between confused seeing and
pure vision, the difference is real.

281
00:16:49,441 --> 00:16:51,901
Physics has its own many worlds.

282
00:16:51,981 --> 00:16:55,122
In Hugh Everett's interpretation
of quantum mechanics,

283
00:16:55,202 --> 00:16:59,813
a single universal quantum state
evolves without ever collapsing.

284
00:16:59,903 --> 00:17:05,054
Through a process called decoherence,
it divides into branches that no longer

285
00:17:05,134 --> 00:17:08,083
affect each other, each
with its own outcome.

286
00:17:08,163 --> 00:17:10,869
The branches are not places side by side.

287
00:17:10,949 --> 00:17:13,509
And the theory is fully deterministic.

288
00:17:14,326 --> 00:17:18,187
Both views reject the picture
of one world seen one way.

289
00:17:18,267 --> 00:17:23,227
But most defenders of Everett treat the
universal wavefunction as the one thing

290
00:17:23,307 --> 00:17:24,966
that really exists.

291
00:17:25,046 --> 00:17:29,382
The Middle Way accepts no floor at
all, not even a mathematical one.

292
00:17:29,462 --> 00:17:31,991
Everett's branches split over time.

293
00:17:32,071 --> 00:17:36,044
The worlds of the bowl arise
together with those who live in them.

294
00:17:36,853 --> 00:17:40,536
Many Buddhist traditions have
explored these many worlds,

295
00:17:40,616 --> 00:17:42,497
and they do not all agree.

296
00:17:43,313 --> 00:17:47,852
The Abhidharma says that the variety
of the world is born of action.

297
00:17:47,932 --> 00:17:53,437
Yogācāra explains shared worlds as
shared karma ripening in consciousness,

298
00:17:53,517 --> 00:17:57,694
though it makes consciousness the
floor that Candrakīrti refused.

299
00:17:58,522 --> 00:18:04,058
The Huayan school pictures Indra's
Net: a net with a jewel at every knot,

300
00:18:04,161 --> 00:18:08,660
each jewel reflecting all the others,
and none of them the original.

301
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:11,893
A thing with a core of its
own would exclude others.

302
00:18:11,973 --> 00:18:15,806
Nothing has one, and so
nothing crowds anything out.

303
00:18:15,886 --> 00:18:19,027
The Tiantai school teaches
that the ten realms,

304
00:18:19,107 --> 00:18:23,963
from hell to buddhahood, are present
in each single moment of mind.

305
00:18:24,769 --> 00:18:29,770
In the Vimalakīrti Sūtra, a disciple
wonders why the Buddha's land looks so

306
00:18:29,850 --> 00:18:33,412
impure. The Buddha touches
the ground with his toe,

307
00:18:33,492 --> 00:18:38,371
and the same land shines as a
jewelled pure land. It was always so.

308
00:18:38,451 --> 00:18:40,314
The disciple had not seen it.

309
00:18:40,394 --> 00:18:43,248
Vajrayāna trains this as pure vision.

310
00:18:43,328 --> 00:18:48,348
And Dzogchen calls the openness of
appearing unimpeded and transparent.

311
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:51,862
These traditions share three things.

312
00:18:51,942 --> 00:18:54,376
Worlds are shaped by
those who live in them.

313
00:18:54,456 --> 00:18:56,699
Worlds need not obstruct one another.

314
00:18:56,779 --> 00:19:00,694
And transformation is a change
in seeing, not a journey.

315
00:19:00,774 --> 00:19:03,832
What they do not share is the
answer about a foundation.

316
00:19:03,912 --> 00:19:08,741
The reading here chooses no foundation,
for the reasons we have followed.

317
00:19:09,561 --> 00:19:12,415
It is worth saying plainly
what has not been shown.

318
00:19:12,495 --> 00:19:15,246
None of this proves
that other realms exist.

319
00:19:15,335 --> 00:19:17,062
Physics does not confirm it.

320
00:19:17,142 --> 00:19:19,576
It is not a theory that predicts anything.

321
00:19:19,656 --> 00:19:23,829
It is not idealism, because
worlds are not inside minds.

322
00:19:23,909 --> 00:19:27,008
And it is one reading
within a living tradition.

323
00:19:27,088 --> 00:19:32,932
What it removes is one confusion: the
idea of a single hidden original beneath

324
00:19:33,012 --> 00:19:34,322
all the worlds.

325
00:19:35,125 --> 00:19:38,306
What difference does it
make? Humility, first.

326
00:19:38,386 --> 00:19:41,118
What we see is not the
measure of all there is.

327
00:19:41,198 --> 00:19:44,895
Every creature we meet,
from a bee to a stranger,

328
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:47,875
lives in a world we cannot fully enter.

329
00:19:48,689 --> 00:19:53,052
And compassion. If the ghost's
pus is really pus for the ghost,

330
00:19:53,132 --> 00:19:56,299
its suffering is not a
mistake to be explained away.

331
00:19:56,379 --> 00:19:59,573
The same holds, with
no appeal to tradition,

332
00:19:59,653 --> 00:20:05,144
for an animal's fear, or the loneliness
of a person whose world we do not share.

333
00:20:05,224 --> 00:20:10,755
No point of view owns the real world, so
no being's world can be dismissed as only

334
00:20:10,835 --> 00:20:14,736
theirs. Emptiness takes nothing
away from their suffering,

335
00:20:14,816 --> 00:20:16,765
or from the wish to relieve it.

336
00:20:17,565 --> 00:20:20,827
Nāgārjuna answered his
critics in one line.

337
00:20:20,907 --> 00:20:24,061
For whom emptiness
works, everything works.

338
00:20:24,141 --> 00:20:27,023
A world of fixed natures
could never change.

339
00:20:27,103 --> 00:20:30,315
Only where nothing is fixed
can anything move at all.

340
00:20:31,129 --> 00:20:35,628
And from the side of Dzogchen: when
appearing is recognised as display,

341
00:20:35,708 --> 00:20:38,956
with no solid self grasping a solid world,

342
00:20:39,036 --> 00:20:41,361
it is met as it always was.

343
00:20:41,441 --> 00:20:44,599
Vivid, unproduced, and found nowhere.

344
00:20:45,413 --> 00:20:49,042
Many worlds, then, and
no floor beneath them.

345
00:20:49,122 --> 00:20:51,315
Everyday life never needed one.

